+## 5. Reverse-mode carrier restrictions (correction item 5)
+
+Pinned-source rule — `needs_udp_to_warp()` (lib.rs L3007–3013): a protocol that needs
+UDP to reach WARP cannot pass a TCP-only carrier:
+
+| Carrier context | WireGuard | GOOL Classic | MASQUE | GOOL (non-classic) | MIM |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **Tor Reverse** (`--tor-reverse`) | **refused** (lib.rs L203–218) | **refused** | **allowed — forced over HTTP/2** (`AETHER_MASQUE_HTTP2=1`, lib.rs L216) | allowed (rides the MASQUE outer hop) | allowed (`needs_udp_to_warp`=false) |
+| **Psiphon Reverse** (`--psiphon-reverse`) | **refused** (lib.rs L229–244) | **refused** | **allowed — forced over HTTP/2** (lib.rs L242) | allowed | allowed |
+| Tor Only / Psiphon Only | n/a (no tunnel) | n/a | n/a | n/a | n/a |
+
+The refusal is explicit and fail-closed (hard error, not a silent substitution) —
+lib.rs L206–213/L232–239: *"… carries tcp only and warp's wireguard endpoints answer
+on udp alone, so {protocol} can never be reached through …"*.
+
+**SMART AUTO obligations (binding):** AUTO must never propose an incompatible
+combination; no restriction may be bypassed by hidden protocol switching, hidden mode
+switching, or a hidden fallback to Direct. Detail in `docs/SMART_AUTO_SPEC.md` §4–§5.
+
